{"id": "EUVD-2026-49312", "enisaUuid": "58f034a8-a358-3120-84a0-3782e7918f8f", "description": "vBulletin 5.x through 5.7.5 and 6.x through 6.2.1 contains an eval injection vulnerability in the vB5_Template_Runtime::runMaths() method within the template runtime that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to execute arbitrary PHP code by supplying crafted input through the pagenav[pagenumber] parameter. Attackers can exploit the insufficiently restrictive regex filter by using phpfuck-style encoding with permitted characters to inject and execute arbitrary PHP code via the unauthenticated ajax/render template route without any authentication.", "datePublished": "2026-07-27T12:39:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T03:56:22", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://karmainsecurity.com/KIS-2026-13", "https://ssd-disclosure.com/vbulletin-runtime-template-runmaths-preauth-rce/", "https://forum.vbulletin.com/forum/vbulletin-announcements/vbulletin-announcements_aa/4509358-security-patch-released-for-vbulletin-6-2-1-6-2-0-and-6-1-6", "https://forum.vbulletin.com/forum/vbulletin-announcements/vbulletin-announcements_aa/4509404-vbulletin-6-2-2-is-available", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vbulletin-eval-injection-rce-via-vb5-template-runtime-php"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-61511", "GHSA-43hg-f3wj-j2m6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 5.61, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3acacdb2-6a74-3c9a-98ee-08612fc868c3", "product": {"name": "vBulletin", "vendor": {"name": "vBulletin"}}, "product_version": "6.0.0 \u22646.2.1"}, {"id": "680351e2-6184-318b-8a32-7e1cf9860484", "product": {"name": "vBulletin", "vendor": {"name": "vBulletin"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.2.2"}, {"id": "a6f6aa7d-ad9c-3e83-a2a8-bf375134cbf5", "product": {"name": "vBulletin", "vendor": {"name": "vBulletin"}}, "product_version": "5.0.0 \u22645.7.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d89b87d5-be58-3aaa-b943